From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: ProgramW6432Dir and CommonW6432Dir in the 32-bit registry view.

64-bit Windows has ProgramW6432Dir and CommonW6432Dir in both registry views; Wine
had them only in the 64-bit one. A 32-bit installer finds
where 64-bit programs go by them: the Qt Installer Framework's @ApplicationsDirX64@
read nothing, and Avidemux's setup offered "\Avidemux 2.8 VC++ 64bits" ("path not
valid").
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index 44cdb24..89f7c9f 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -665,6 +665,11 @@ HKLM,Software\Microsoft\Wow64\x86,,2,"xtajit.dll"
 [CurrentVersionWow64.ntx86]
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramFilesDir (x86)",,"%16422%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonFilesDir (x86)",,"%16427%"
+; Stained Glass OS: the 64-bit directories in the 32-bit view too, as 64-bit Windows has them
+; there: a 32-bit installer finds where 64-bit programs go by them (Qt Installer Framework's
+; @ApplicationsDirX64@, Avidemux's setup)
+HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramW6432Dir",,"C:\Program Files"
+HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonW6432Dir",,"C:\Program Files\Common Files"
 
 [CurrentVersionWow64.ntarm]
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramFilesDir (Arm)",,"%16422%"
